THOUGHT: The PASS_NULLABLE error is because `filter(endpoint, zuulReq)` is annotated as possibly returning null, while `invokeNextStage` requires a non-null `HttpResponseMessage`. In the other `filter(HttpRequestMessage)` method, they already guard against null by assigning the result to a local variable and checking it before calling `invokeNextStage`. I should mirror that pattern here: store the result of `filter(endpoint, zuulReq)` in a local variable, check for null, and only call `invokeNextStage` when it’s non-null. This avoids passing a nullable value and preserves existing behavior. After editing the file, I’ll run the NullAway compilation to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/zuul && sed -i '160,164c\          // whole body has arrived, resume filter chain
          ByteBufUtil.touch(
              newChunk, "Endpoint body complete, resume chain, ZuulMessage: ", zuulReq);
          final HttpResponseMessage zuulResp = filter(endpoint, zuulReq);
          if (zuulResp != null) {
            invokeNextStage(zuulResp);
          }' zuul-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/zuul/netty/filter/ZuulEndPointRunner.java && ./gradlew zuul-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

